{"surah": 105, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصْحَٰبِ ٱلْفِيلِ ", "translation": "Have you not considered, [O Muḥammad], how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَرَ", "translit": "َrَt", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَعَلَ", "translit": "َlَʿعَf", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِأَصْحَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰḥْṣَaʾِb", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْفِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِfْlٱ", "root": "فيل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "أَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ كَيْدَهُمْ فِى تَضْلِيلٍ ", "translation": "Did He not make their plan into misguidance?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَجْعَلْ", "translit": "ْlَʿعْjgَy", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْدَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَضْلِيلٍ", "translit": "ٍlyِlْḍَt", "root": "ضلل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَأَرْسَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ طَيْرًا أَبَابِيلَ ", "translation": "And He sent against them birds in flocks,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَرْسَلَ", "translit": "َlَsْrَaʾَw", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "طَيْرًا", "translit": "āًrْyَṭ", "root": "طير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَبَابِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِbāَbَaʾ", "root": "ابل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "تَرْمِيهِم بِحِجَارَةٍ مِّن سِجِّيلٍ ", "translation": "Striking them with stones of hard clay,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَرْمِيهِم", "translit": "mِhyِmْrَt", "root": "رمي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِحِجَارَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَrāَjgِḥِb", "root": "حجر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سِجِّيلٍ", "translit": "ٍlyِّjgِs", "root": "سجل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "فَجَعَلَهُمْ كَعَصْفٍ مَّأْكُولٍۭ ", "translation": "And He made them like eaten straw.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَجَعَلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَʿعَjgَf", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَعَصْفٍ", "translit": "ٍfْṣَʿعَk", "root": "عصف"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّأْكُولٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭlwُkْaʾَّm", "root": "اكل"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "تر كيف فعل ربك بعاد إرم ذات العماد ألم تر كيف فعل ربك بأصحاب الفيل ولايعدو القرآن هذه الأقسام الثلاثة وهي الإرشاد إلى معرفة ذات الله وتقديسه أو معرفة صفاته وأسمائه أو معرفة أفعاله وسنته مع عباده ولما اشتملت سورة الإخلاص على أحد هذه الأقسام الثلاثة وهو التقديس وازنها رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم بثلث القرآن فقال من قرأ سورة الإخلاص فقد قرأ ثلث القرآن (1) حديث دعائه لابن عباس اللهم فقهه في الدين وعلمه التأويل متفق عليه دون قوله وعلمه التأويل ورواه أحمد بهذه الزيادة وتقدم في العلم القول في معنى الرضا بقضاء ا", "english": "And in the report [it is said]: Verily God—exalted is He—revealed to a servant whom He had taken by the hand after he had been on the brink of destruction: \"How many a sin did you commit against Me, and I forgave it for you—sins for the sake of which I destroyed entire nations among the nations!\" So this is the way (sunnah) of God—exalted is He—with His servants, by way of favor (tafḍīl), and bringing forward (taqdīm), and deferring (taʾkhīr), according to what the eternal will (al-mashīʾah al-azaliyyah) had previously decreed.", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "section_title_ar": "Section 1188", "section_title_en": "On the Meaning of Contentment with God's Decree (Al-Riḍā bi Qaḍāʾ Allāh), Its Reality, and What Has Been Reported Concerning Its Virtue", "section_index": 1188, "anchors": "- Root: رضي (Raḍā)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of being pleased, satisfied, consenting; the opposite of anger (sakhaṭ). Its object is that which is agreeable and harmonious with one's will.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Raḍā is a state of the heart (ḥāl min aḥwāl al-qalb) signifying the soul's inclination toward what is pleasing, and its cessation of opposition. In theological terms, it is the soul's acquiescence to the divine decree (qaḍāʾ) after the removal of inner resistance.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"رَضِيَ عَنْهُ\" — to be content with someone. Metaphorical (majāz): \"رَضِيَ بِالكَوْنِ\" — submission to what is, even when it opposes the appetites, which is the higher spiritual usage.\n- Root: قضي (Qaḍā)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To decree, determine, execute, or finish a matter; the cutting off of a thing decisively.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Qaḍāʾ is the divine determination (taqdīr) and execution of affairs according to prior eternal knowledge; it encompasses both what is feared and what is hoped for.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the completion of a judgment. Metaphorical: the divine decree as the all-encompassing will of God, which the believer must embrace.\n- Root: ولي (Waliya)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Nearness, guardianship, and governance; the one who manages affairs.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Walī is the one who is near to God through obedience, and God is the Walī of the believer through grace and protection.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: proximity. Metaphorical: friendship and divine patronage.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Predicate Emphasis (Bāb al-Taʾkīd bi al-Ḍamīr al-Munfaṣil) — The repetition of the pronoun for emphasis, as in \"اللهُ هُوَ\" structures, to affirm the exclusivity of divine attributes without ambiguity.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Hadith"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 400, 1148], [2, 1148, 1615], [3, 1615, 2456], [4, 2456, 3216], [5, 3216, 4093], [6, 4093, 5596], [7, 5596, 6940]], "105:1": [[1, 400, 1148], [2, 1148, 1615], [3, 1615, 2456], [4, 2456, 3216], [5, 3216, 4093], [6, 4093, 5596], [7, 5596, 6940]], "2": [[1, 450, 1154], [2, 1154, 2463], [3, 2463, 3673], [4, 3673, 4245], [5, 4245, 5710]], "105:2": [[1, 450, 1154], [2, 1154, 2463], [3, 2463, 3673], [4, 3673, 4245], [5, 4245, 5710]], "3": [[1, 280, 1566], [2, 1566, 2669], [3, 2669, 3926], [4, 3926, 5710]], "105:3": [[1, 280, 1566], [2, 1566, 2669], [3, 2669, 3926], [4, 3926, 5710]], "4": [[1, 180, 2243], [2, 2243, 4390], [3, 4390, 5294], [4, 5294, 7060]], "105:4": [[1, 180, 2243], [2, 2243, 4390], [3, 4390, 5294], [4, 5294, 7060]], "5": [[1, 220, 1903], [2, 1903, 3135], [3, 3135, 5270]], "105:5": [[1, 220, 1903], [2, 1903, 3135], [3, 3135, 5270]]}, "abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 0, 1150], [2, 1150, 1690], [3, 1690, 2340], [4, 2340, 3040], [5, 3040, 3950], [6, 3950, 5210], [7, 5210, 6275]], "105:1": [[1, 0, 1150], [2, 1150, 1690], [3, 1690, 2340], [4, 2340, 3040], [5, 3040, 3950], [6, 3950, 5210], [7, 5210, 6275]], "2": [[1, 0, 1100], [2, 1100, 1980], [3, 1980, 3040], [4, 3040, 3570], [5, 3570, 4695]], "105:2": [[1, 0, 1100], [2, 1100, 1980], [3, 1980, 3040], [4, 3040, 3570], [5, 3570, 4695]], "3": [[1, 0, 1470], [2, 1470, 2540], [3, 2540, 3460], [4, 3460, 4905]], "105:3": [[1, 0, 1470], [2, 1470, 2540], [3, 2540, 3460], [4, 3460, 4905]], "4": [[1, 0, 2470], [2, 2470, 4958], [3, 4958, 6022], [4, 6022, 7265]], "105:4": [[1, 0, 2470], [2, 2470, 4958], [3, 4958, 6022], [4, 6022, 7265]], "5": [[1, 0, 1680], [2, 1680, 3369], [3, 3369, 4595]], "105:5": [[1, 0, 1680], [2, 1680, 3369], [3, 3369, 4595]]}, "abdulbasit_mujawwad": {"1": [[1, 1550, 2410], [2, 2420, 3160], [3, 3170, 4430], [4, 4440, 5650], [5, 5660, 7330], [6, 7340, 9770], [7, 9780, 14050]], "105:1": [[1, 1550, 2410], [2, 2420, 3160], [3, 3170, 4430], [4, 4440, 5650], [5, 5660, 7330], [6, 7340, 9770], [7, 9780, 14050]], "2": [[1, 3150, 3720], [2, 3730, 5330], [3, 5340, 7230], [4, 7240, 8070], [5, 8080, 10160]], "105:2": [[1, 31